      "slug": "moss-stitch-g46",
      "term": "Moss stitch",
      "definition": "A two-row pattern: row 1 works dc and chain 1 alternately; row 2 works dc into each chain space and chain 1 into each dc. The offset columns create a tight, woven-looking texture."
    },
    {
      "slug": "turning-ch-g46",
      "term": "Turning chain",
      "definition": "The chain worked at the end of a row before turning. On a moss stitch row, the turning chain is usually chain 1 and does not count as a stitch."
    }
  ],
